-- title:
--   Coefficientwise compatibility of base-changed q-expansion automorphisms
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ and $L'$ be fields equipped with $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structures and with an $L$-algebra structure on $L'$ compatible with these (a scalar tower over $\mathbb{Q}$), both $L$ and $L'$ algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q)) =$ `LaurentSeries ℚ` over $\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\sigma_0$ be a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism of $F_0$. For a field $K$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange K F₀`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) denotes the intermediate field of `LaurentSeries K` over $K$ generated by the image of $F_0$ under the coefficientwise ring map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb K`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to K$, and [`ModularCurve.baseChangeAut K σ₀`](def/ModularCurve_X1Diamond.html#L24) denotes a choice, if one exists, of a $K$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of that field with $\sigma(\mathrm{coeffEmb}_K\, y) = \mathrm{coeffEmb}_K(\sigma_0 y)$ for all $y \in F_0$, and the identity otherwise. Given $b$ in `laurentBaseChange L F₀` and $b'$ in `laurentBaseChange L' F₀` whose underlying Laurent series satisfy $b' = \mathrm{coeffMap}(L \to L')(b)$, where [`ModularCurve.coeffMap`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L16) applies a ring homomorphism to each coefficient, the conclusion is the corresponding identity of Laurent series over $L'$ for the images: $(\mathrm{baseChangeAut}_{L'}\sigma_0)(b') = \mathrm{coeffMap}(L \to L')\bigl((\mathrm{baseChangeAut}_L\sigma_0)(b)\bigr)$.
--
--   This records that the base change to $L$ of an automorphism of a field of $q$-expansions over $\mathbb{Q}$ is compatible, coefficientwise, with enlarging the field of constants from $L$ to an algebraic extension $L'$. It is used when a diamond automorphism of the function field of $X_1(N)$ over a small algebraic field is compared with its counterpart over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, in the construction of the reduction data for $X_1(N)$ entering the Frey curve argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_coe_baseChangeAut_eq_coeffMap_coe_baseChangeAut_of_coe_eq_coeffMap.lean

